From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Johansen <john.johansen@canonical.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Jan 2026 10:10:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: apparmor5.1.0 [24/25]: apparmor: skb: add the
 ability to use interface in network mediation.

BugLink: http://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2144679

Add the ability to mediate network connections at the interface and
packet level. This extends AppArmor network mediation to be able to
interact with firewalls through the secmark, and restrict applications
to use only approved network interfaces.

Because per packet mediation can have a higher cost, it is only applied
when profiles or fire wall rules are added that set the secmark, or
if apparmor rules require interface mediation.

The mediation is placed behind a new abi so that it is not applied
with older policy.

Signed-off-by: John Johansen <john.johansen@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00242
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@fd725febe64c2139b07b35e09f2cea9f20ffb405
